1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:01,633
<i>What? You think I didn't notice</i>

2
00:00:01,767 --> 00:00:02,867
<i>that you're making moves
on my daughter?</i>

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,367
<i> You're even sucking up to me!</i>

4
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,333
<i> So, may the best man win.</i>

5
00:00:06,467 --> 00:00:08,067
<i> You're ruining my move!</i>

6
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:09,200
<i> Well, I'm just trying</i>

7
00:00:09,333 --> 00:00:10,733
<i> to patch things up with Joey.</i>

8
00:00:10,867 --> 00:00:13,567
<i>That's why we're here,
hiding from the syndicate.</i>

9
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:14,833
<i> Where are you going again?</i>

10
00:00:14,967 --> 00:00:16,200
<i>If you don't want me to go out,</i>

11
00:00:16,333 --> 00:00:17,900
<i> then you buy what I need.</i>

12
00:00:18,033 --> 00:00:19,433
<i> I have this fear...</i>

13
00:00:19,567 --> 00:00:20,967
<i> that I'll lose you someday.</i>

14
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:22,600
<i> Do we have enemies here?</i>

15
00:00:22,733 --> 00:00:24,367
<i> Yes, those three fools!</i>

16
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:25,900
<i>Good thing we're okay now,
right?</i>

17
00:00:26,033 --> 00:00:27,300
<i> I hope it's always like this.</i>

18
00:00:27,433 --> 00:00:28,800
<i> Like we don't have problems.</i>

19
00:00:28,933 --> 00:00:30,000
<i> What are you doing here?</i>

20
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:31,200
<i> We only have one problem.</i>

21
00:00:31,333 --> 00:00:32,367
<i> What is it this time?</i>

22
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:33,700
<i> The one you told us to watch</i>

23
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:35,200
<i>seems to be plotting something.</i>

24
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:37,867
<i>If she tries,
I'll kill her myself.</i>

25
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,167
<i> You'll kill someone?</i>

26
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:40,367
<i> It was just an expression.</i>

27
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:42,600
<i>Tomas, be careful
with what you say.</i>

28
00:00:42,733 --> 00:00:43,667
<i> Can you just let it go?</i>

29
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,267
<i> And don't ever dictate to me!</i>

30
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:47,300
<i>What happened to
the one Cruz spoke with?</i>

31
00:00:47,433 --> 00:00:48,333
<i> Can't be contacted anymore.</i>

32
00:00:48,467 --> 00:00:49,333
<i> Did Cruz identify</i>

33
00:00:49,467 --> 00:00:50,867
<i> who called the hotline?</i>

34
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,500
<i>- [SCREAMS]
- Liza De Leon.</i>

35
00:00:52,633 --> 00:00:54,100
<i> I hope you're right, Jin Ho.</i>

36
00:00:54,233 --> 00:00:54,967
<i> I don't know when,</i>

37
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:56,100
<i> I don't know where.</i>

38
00:00:56,233 --> 00:00:58,233
<i>But I'm sure
of my feelings for you.</i>

39
00:00:58,367 --> 00:00:59,667
<i> I love you, Joey.</i>

40
00:01:02,767 --> 00:01:05,033
<i> [OBB]</i>

41
00:01:19,067 --> 00:01:20,300
What?

42
00:01:21,333 --> 00:01:23,100
But when I confessed to you...

43
00:01:23,233 --> 00:01:24,500
Yes, I know.

44
00:01:24,633 --> 00:01:27,433
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

45
00:01:27,567 --> 00:01:29,067
Joey, I'm...

46
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:32,000
I'm sorry, I hurt you,
I know.

47
00:01:32,133 --> 00:01:34,900
I thought we couldn't work.

48
00:01:35,033 --> 00:01:36,400
That it was impossible...

49
00:01:36,533 --> 00:01:39,700
because you're young,
we're different.

50
00:01:41,167 --> 00:01:43,000
I know I hurt you,

51
00:01:44,233 --> 00:01:45,433
and I'm sorry.

52
00:01:45,567 --> 00:01:48,133
I'll make it up to you, please.

53
00:01:48,267 --> 00:01:50,000
We're okay now, right?

54
00:01:50,533 --> 00:01:51,933
Why are you complicating things?

55
00:01:52,067 --> 00:01:54,567
Joey, I'm just being honest
with you now.

56
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:56,400
What do you want me to say?

57
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:00,100
That we're okay?
That we can be a couple?

58
00:02:02,433 --> 00:02:04,267
Didn't you reject me

59
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:06,100
when I confessed before?

60
00:02:06,233 --> 00:02:07,300
And I accepted that.

61
00:02:07,433 --> 00:02:08,900
I moved on.

62
00:02:10,333 --> 00:02:12,800
And now you're telling me
you love me?

63
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,200
It feels like
you're playing with my feelings.

64
00:02:16,867 --> 00:02:17,800
Joey, it's not like that.

65
00:02:17,933 --> 00:02:20,233
That's not what I wanted
to happen.

66
00:02:21,633 --> 00:02:23,733
But that's what I feel.

67
00:02:23,867 --> 00:02:28,500
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

68
00:02:29,833 --> 00:02:31,367
Joey!

69
00:02:35,667 --> 00:02:38,867
- [WHIP WHACKS]
- Enough! Enough!

70
00:02:41,333 --> 00:02:44,433
- [WHIP WHACKS]
- [GROANS AND BAWLS]

71
00:02:44,567 --> 00:02:45,800
You snake!

72
00:02:45,933 --> 00:02:48,800
[GROANING]

73
00:02:48,967 --> 00:02:50,167
Enough!

74
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:52,933
[BAWLS]

75
00:02:53,067 --> 00:02:56,133
- [WHIP WHACKS]
- [GROANS AND BAWLS]

76
00:02:58,033 --> 00:03:00,533
Enough!

77
00:03:01,433 --> 00:03:05,200
Enough! Enough, Berdugo! Enough!

78
00:03:05,333 --> 00:03:08,333
Please, have mercy, enough!

79
00:03:13,733 --> 00:03:16,067
You think you can fool us, huh.

80
00:03:18,767 --> 00:03:20,967
We know your plans!

81
00:03:23,167 --> 00:03:24,733
Stop it...

82
00:03:24,867 --> 00:03:26,333
Please, have mercy, stop it.

83
00:03:26,467 --> 00:03:27,500
Let me go.

84
00:03:27,633 --> 00:03:29,400
I didn't do anything.

85
00:03:29,533 --> 00:03:31,600
What are you talking about?

86
00:03:31,733 --> 00:03:34,167
I didn't do anything!

87
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:37,233
That's what a guilty person
usually says.

88
00:03:37,367 --> 00:03:38,667
[SOBBING]

89
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,300
I saw your phone.

90
00:03:40,433 --> 00:03:42,133
But we just wanted to make sure

91
00:03:42,267 --> 00:03:45,167
you won't carry out your plans!

92
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:46,800
So? Is that ready?

93
00:03:46,933 --> 00:03:49,700
<i>Make sure Liza's car
doesn't stop, okay?</i>

94
00:03:49,833 --> 00:03:51,267
<i> Yes, Boss.</i>

95
00:03:52,633 --> 00:03:54,700
Berdugo, enough.
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:03:56,567 --> 00:03:57,933
[WHINES]

97
00:03:58,067 --> 00:03:59,433
Honestly...

98
00:03:59,567 --> 00:04:01,400
I told Matias

99
00:04:01,533 --> 00:04:03,267
maybe his suspicion was wrong.

100
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:05,000
That's why I need proof.

101
00:04:05,133 --> 00:04:08,333
I said, if Liza leaves,

102
00:04:08,467 --> 00:04:11,233
it means she'll betray us.

103
00:04:11,367 --> 00:04:13,400
It was a test...

104
00:04:15,467 --> 00:04:17,100
of loyalty.

105
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,067
Have mercy, Berdugo.

106
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:23,867
And you failed!

107
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:27,200
You know what happens

108
00:04:27,367 --> 00:04:29,933
to those who betray me, right?

109
00:04:30,367 --> 00:04:32,000
Enough...

110
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:37,400
Enough...

111
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:39,767
I didn't do anything.

112
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:41,400
Let me go.

113
00:04:41,533 --> 00:04:42,600
Please have mercy!

114
00:04:42,733 --> 00:04:45,367
Please, help me!

115
00:04:46,433 --> 00:04:49,300
Okay, Chief, I'll call later.

116
00:04:55,333 --> 00:04:57,133
So, Oppa? Are you okay?

117
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:02,267
Joey, wait, wait.

118
00:05:03,133 --> 00:05:04,567
Ah...

119
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:06,400
Dad, what's happening?

120
00:05:06,533 --> 00:05:08,433
Liza was supposed to surrender.

121
00:05:08,567 --> 00:05:09,933
But she didn't show up.

122
00:05:10,067 --> 00:05:11,867
So, Jin Ho is worried.

123
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,533
Why would he worry?

124
00:05:15,733 --> 00:05:18,467
Something bad
must have happened to her.

125
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:21,600
That's why she didn't show up.

126
00:05:21,733 --> 00:05:23,833
I know where she might be.

127
00:05:23,967 --> 00:05:26,200
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

128
00:05:26,333 --> 00:05:27,700
Sir...

129
00:05:27,833 --> 00:05:30,167
I want to help you find Berdugo.

130
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:34,700
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

131
00:05:37,033 --> 00:05:41,067
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

132
00:05:43,233 --> 00:05:45,700
<i> Yes, I got the location map.</i>

133
00:05:45,833 --> 00:05:47,067
<i> Thank you.</i>

134
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:51,233
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

135
00:06:04,067 --> 00:06:08,767
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

136
00:06:16,133 --> 00:06:17,667
Probably there.

137
00:06:18,467 --> 00:06:20,467
This place looks big.

138
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:22,467
That's the only place I know

139
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:25,033
since they don't trust me much.

140
00:06:25,167 --> 00:06:28,267
That means your group
doesn't accept you.

141
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:31,267
But we'll still try.

142
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:33,133
I'll just call Chief.

143
00:06:37,733 --> 00:06:40,133
You're already excluded there,
why join them?

144
00:06:40,267 --> 00:06:42,500
We're here, your friends.

145
00:06:42,667 --> 00:06:44,200
He's doing it for Liza.

146
00:06:44,333 --> 00:06:46,433
Because if you love someone,

147
00:06:46,567 --> 00:06:48,433
you're willing to take a risk.

148
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:54,767
I wanted to protect Liza
and you guys too.

149
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:56,633
That's why I stayed.

150
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:03,033
Do you really have
to talk to her like that?

151
00:07:03,167 --> 00:07:05,500
He's already stressed.

152
00:07:07,367 --> 00:07:09,600
Joey! Oppa!

153
00:07:11,967 --> 00:07:14,533
Do you and Joey have a problem?

154
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:16,567
None.

155
00:07:22,267 --> 00:07:25,033
- [WHIP WHACKS]
- [GROANS AND BAWLS]

156
00:07:25,167 --> 00:07:26,200
Enough!

157
00:07:26,333 --> 00:07:29,500
- [WHIP WHACKS]
- [GROANS AND BAWLS]

158
00:07:29,633 --> 00:07:33,600
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

159
00:07:36,433 --> 00:07:38,600
We're done talking, Liza.

160
00:07:38,733 --> 00:07:41,367
You can't be trusted!

161
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:43,500
Whatever you say,

162
00:07:43,633 --> 00:07:45,967
consider it your last words!

163
00:07:46,433 --> 00:07:49,833
I helped grow this organization.

164
00:07:50,433 --> 00:07:52,733
I brought millions!

165
00:07:53,433 --> 00:07:55,100
Why would I do that to you!

166
00:07:55,233 --> 00:07:57,633
Why would I betray you?

167
00:07:57,767 --> 00:07:58,767
Enough, Berdugo.

168
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:00,733
Please, have mercy.

169
00:08:00,867 --> 00:08:04,333
Don't hurt me anymore, please.

170
00:08:04,867 --> 00:08:06,767
- Please, have mercy.
- Fine.

171
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:09,267
I won't hurt you anymore.

172
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:13,367
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

173
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,400
- [WHIP WHACKS]
- [GROANS AND BAWLS]

174
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:31,233
- [WHIP WHACKS]
- [GROANS AND BAWLS]

175
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:34,100
Joey, Joey, teka.

176
00:08:34,233 --> 00:08:35,433
We have nothing else
to talk about now

177
00:08:35,567 --> 00:08:37,333
but our friend's situation.

178
00:08:37,467 --> 00:08:38,733
So please don't bring up

179
00:08:38,867 --> 00:08:40,800
wanting us to be together.

180
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:42,967
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

181
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:44,833
You got great timing.

182
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,367
Jin Ho...

183
00:09:01,067 --> 00:09:03,233
Look. I'm sorry for
what I said earlier.

184
00:09:04,133 --> 00:09:05,967
Are you okay, Jin Ho?

185
00:09:31,667 --> 00:09:34,700
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

186
00:09:37,467 --> 00:09:39,533
Jin Ho, don't lose hope.

187
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:43,633
Just trust, Jin Ho.

188
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:46,967
I'm sure dad will help too.

189
00:09:47,100 --> 00:09:50,900
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

190
00:09:51,367 --> 00:09:53,367
We need help.

191
00:09:53,667 --> 00:09:54,833
The place is big.

192
00:09:55,233 --> 00:09:56,767
There's a lot to guard.

193
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:59,400
We need to verify
this info first.

194
00:09:59,533 --> 00:10:02,133
But I'll coordinate
with other precincts,

195
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:05,967
<i> maybe they can send their men.</i>

196
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:08,933
Chief, can I take a break first?

197
00:10:09,067 --> 00:10:10,333
Why?

198
00:10:10,467 --> 00:10:12,367
<i>I've been through
a lot with this person.</i>

199
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:14,933
I want to be the one
to catch him myself.

200
00:10:15,633 --> 00:10:17,800
<i>All right, I'll send Cruz there.</i>

201
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,400
- Salazar.
- Sir?

202
00:10:21,533 --> 00:10:22,600
Call Cruz.

203
00:10:22,733 --> 00:10:23,933
Tell him to come to my office.

204
00:10:24,067 --> 00:10:25,533
Yes, Sir.

205
00:10:25,667 --> 00:10:28,967
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

206
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:32,100
Matias, since
you'll handle operations

207
00:10:32,233 --> 00:10:33,267
both in and out,

208
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:34,867
I want everything in order.

209
00:10:35,033 --> 00:10:37,233
I'll take care of it, Berdugo.

210
00:10:37,367 --> 00:10:38,333
Good.

211
00:10:38,467 --> 00:10:39,933
We need to recover...

212
00:10:40,067 --> 00:10:42,267
because we've lost a lot.

213
00:10:42,867 --> 00:10:44,500
I thought of canceling
our meeting

214
00:10:44,633 --> 00:10:47,200
with our client, Mr. Stuart.

215
00:10:47,667 --> 00:10:48,733
Why?

216
00:10:48,867 --> 00:10:50,767
He's one of our top clients.
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

217
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,200
That's the problem,
we're in the hot seat right now.

218
00:10:53,867 --> 00:10:55,400
They might lose trust

219
00:10:55,533 --> 00:10:58,000
if they see we're careless.

220
00:10:58,133 --> 00:11:00,700
There's a bigger chance
they'll back out

221
00:11:00,833 --> 00:11:01,667
if they find out...

222
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:04,067
we don't control the situation.

223
00:11:05,333 --> 00:11:07,833
So, where will you
hold the meeting?

224
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,033
The radar's still hot.

225
00:11:10,667 --> 00:11:12,100
Don't cancel.

226
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:14,500
I have a plan.

227
00:11:15,533 --> 00:11:18,733
Cruz will go with you
while I'm gone.

228
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:21,600
Whatever he says, follow it.

229
00:11:21,733 --> 00:11:22,633
Clear?

230
00:11:22,767 --> 00:11:24,233
Sir, yes, Sir!

231
00:11:24,933 --> 00:11:26,467
Major, will we be here for long?

232
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:29,533
Well, hopefully, with the info
we got from Jin Ho,

233
00:11:29,667 --> 00:11:31,900
this will all end.

234
00:11:32,033 --> 00:11:34,367
Dad, Jin Ho
and I are begging you,

235
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:36,933
if you see Liza,

236
00:11:37,067 --> 00:11:38,967
please don't hurt her.

237
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:40,967
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

238
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:44,167
Jin Ho, that's also what my
daughter told me when...

239
00:11:44,333 --> 00:11:46,433
we caught you,

240
00:11:46,567 --> 00:11:48,267
not to hurt you.

241
00:11:49,967 --> 00:11:52,400
Joey, thank you.

242
00:11:54,233 --> 00:11:56,067
Don't worry, I'll do everything

243
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:58,367
to keep her safe.

244
00:11:58,500 --> 00:11:59,767
Thank you, Dad.

245
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:01,800
Thank you, Sir.

246
00:12:01,933 --> 00:12:04,367
Now I know why Joey
is always positive.

247
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:06,267
She got it from you.

248
00:12:08,533 --> 00:12:10,267
Take care.

249
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:13,533
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

250
00:12:14,733 --> 00:12:16,933
[ENGINE STARTS]

251
00:12:17,067 --> 00:12:21,300
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

252
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:42,733
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

253
00:12:47,533 --> 00:12:49,100
I'm sorry.

254
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:53,133
You really scared me.

255
00:12:53,967 --> 00:12:55,033
You really did.

256
00:12:55,167 --> 00:12:56,667
I know.

257
00:12:57,567 --> 00:13:00,033
I've just been
really stressed lately.

258
00:13:00,167 --> 00:13:04,067
And I think you should
take a break

259
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:06,433
if it's affecting you.

260
00:13:06,567 --> 00:13:08,900
You know, it's just work.

261
00:13:10,333 --> 00:13:11,767
You're right.

262
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:13,733
I have an idea.

263
00:13:13,867 --> 00:13:15,100
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

264
00:13:15,233 --> 00:13:18,500
You're right,
I should detach from work

265
00:13:18,633 --> 00:13:20,367
even for a while.

266
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:22,600
And I think the foundation's
groundbreaking event

267
00:13:22,733 --> 00:13:25,500
is the best outlet.

268
00:13:25,633 --> 00:13:27,500
Really?

269
00:13:27,633 --> 00:13:29,067
You'll attend tomorrow?

270
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,600
Yes.

271
00:13:30,733 --> 00:13:34,600
Of course, I want to support
my wife.

272
00:13:34,733 --> 00:13:37,100
And I think this is
the perfect opportunity

273
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:39,033
for the foundation.

274
00:13:39,167 --> 00:13:41,800
so I want to be there
for my wife.

275
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:44,233
Thank you, Hon.

276
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:47,967
Well, I'll prepare
what I'll wear.

277
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:50,767
Ah, where will you
hold this event?

278
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:53,700
Ah, at the old prairie.

279
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:56,233
We bought part
of the land there.

280
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:59,500
With enough donations
and sponsorship,

281
00:13:59,633 --> 00:14:02,233
we'll build the orphanage there.

282
00:14:03,267 --> 00:14:06,133
Well, I'm sure
it will be a success.

283
00:14:06,733 --> 00:14:08,467
Thank you, Hon.

284
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:12,733
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

285
00:14:27,367 --> 00:14:31,400
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

286
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:47,167
Oh...

287
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:50,033
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

288
00:14:50,167 --> 00:14:51,500
Miguel...

289
00:14:52,667 --> 00:14:54,633
you scared me.

290
00:14:54,767 --> 00:14:56,333
I'm sorry.

291
00:14:56,867 --> 00:14:59,367
But wait, what are you
doing here?

292
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:02,367
Weren't you with Joey?

293
00:15:02,533 --> 00:15:04,900
You were safe in hiding,

294
00:15:05,033 --> 00:15:06,067
why did you leave?

295
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:07,133
Did you abandon her?

296
00:15:07,267 --> 00:15:09,100
Don't worry, Cruz is there.

297
00:15:09,233 --> 00:15:10,567
They're safe.

298
00:15:10,700 --> 00:15:13,200
The Korean gave a tip,

299
00:15:13,333 --> 00:15:15,333
that's why I left.

300
00:15:15,467 --> 00:15:19,167
And I want to make sure
we'll be safe

301
00:15:19,933 --> 00:15:21,933
once the syndicate is gone.

302
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:24,600
And when that happens,

303
00:15:24,733 --> 00:15:26,867
you won't have
to be afraid anymore.

304
00:15:30,567 --> 00:15:34,933
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

305
00:15:45,333 --> 00:15:46,767
Oh, Joey...

306
00:15:46,900 --> 00:15:48,567
you woke up early,
coffee?

307
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:49,567
Good morning po.

308
00:15:49,700 --> 00:15:51,200
It's okay, later.

309
00:15:51,733 --> 00:15:53,967
Did dad call already?

310
00:15:54,100 --> 00:15:55,933
Not yet, but I'm sure

311
00:15:56,067 --> 00:15:58,333
Chief is working on it now.

312
00:15:59,033 --> 00:16:00,533
Stay alert.

313
00:16:00,667 --> 00:16:02,067
If you see anything strange,

314
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,400
tell me right away.

315
00:16:03,533 --> 00:16:04,633
Yes, Sir!
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

316
00:16:04,767 --> 00:16:05,633
Turn right there.

317
00:16:05,767 --> 00:16:07,133
Check, maybe
the warehouse is there.

318
00:16:07,267 --> 00:16:08,667
Okay, Sir!

319
00:16:11,933 --> 00:16:13,700
Did Mr. Stuart confirm?

320
00:16:13,833 --> 00:16:15,533
Yes, Berdugo.

321
00:16:15,667 --> 00:16:17,533
He even seemed pleased.

322
00:16:17,667 --> 00:16:20,300
He said the meeting place
felt like a movie set.

323
00:16:20,433 --> 00:16:21,733
That's good.

324
00:16:22,433 --> 00:16:24,933
We need to please our clients.

325
00:16:27,300 --> 00:16:28,667
Is she still alive?

326
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:30,567
Yes, Berdugo.

327
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:43,400
Don't worry, Liza.

328
00:16:43,533 --> 00:16:45,967
I won't prolong your suffering.

329
00:16:51,667 --> 00:16:53,367
Take her with you.

330
00:16:53,500 --> 00:16:55,867
We'll dispose of her
along the way.

331
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:04,133
Go on, carry her now.

332
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:21,467
Good morning.

333
00:17:23,533 --> 00:17:26,000
Good morning, Joey.

334
00:17:26,133 --> 00:17:28,200
Is Jin Ho still asleep?

335
00:17:28,333 --> 00:17:30,467
He's not in his room.

336
00:17:30,600 --> 00:17:33,500
Actually, we thought
he was with you.

337
00:17:34,267 --> 00:17:36,300
What?

338
00:17:36,433 --> 00:17:37,733
Then where is he?

339
00:17:38,433 --> 00:17:40,167
Let's find Jin Ho!

340
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:43,567
- Check upstairs.
- Wait, I'll check upstairs.

341
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:45,900
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

342
00:17:46,033 --> 00:17:48,067
- [PETER SHOUTING IN DISTANCE]
- Jin Ho!

343
00:17:48,933 --> 00:17:50,400
Jin Ho!

344
00:17:50,533 --> 00:17:52,000
[PETER SHOUTING]

345
00:17:54,267 --> 00:17:55,567
- Nothing, he's not there.
- Jin Ho!

346
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:57,467
- Not there?
- Not there.

347
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:59,233
- Jin Ho!
- Huh?

348
00:17:59,367 --> 00:18:00,200
- Not there?
- He's not there.

349
00:18:00,333 --> 00:18:01,267
Let's find him, quick!

350
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,800
- Outside, come on!
- Jin Ho!

351
00:18:02,933 --> 00:18:04,333
Jin Ho!

352
00:18:19,267 --> 00:18:20,867
Isn't there a guard here?

353
00:18:22,533 --> 00:18:24,133
Gonzalo was stationed here.

354
00:18:24,267 --> 00:18:25,467
His motorcycle is gone too.

355
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:27,067
Help!

356
00:18:27,867 --> 00:18:29,233
Help!

357
00:18:30,733 --> 00:18:32,000
Gonzalo, what happened here?

358
00:18:32,133 --> 00:18:34,067
Sir, the Korean escaped.

359
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:36,100
He even took my gun.

360
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:44,033
[REVVING]

361
00:18:44,167 --> 00:18:46,533
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

362
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:49,433
<i> I'm coming for you, Liza.</i>

363
00:18:49,567 --> 00:18:55,367
[REVVING]

364
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:56,867
Thank you.

365
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,700
I'm sure he'll go to Liza.

366
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:00,267
Let's go.

367
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:01,500
Major Delgado told me

368
00:19:01,633 --> 00:19:02,767
when I spoke to him,

369
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:04,467
I should take you home.

370
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:06,567
Peter, you stay
with Major for now.

371
00:19:06,700 --> 00:19:07,867
But what now? We don't know...

372
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,000
what will happen to Jin Ho.

373
00:19:10,133 --> 00:19:11,833
Let's just hope he is okay.

374
00:19:13,433 --> 00:19:14,700
Where could he have gone?

375
00:19:14,833 --> 00:19:16,767
Did Oppa escape again?

376
00:19:17,933 --> 00:19:19,267
I don't think so.

377
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:21,433
I think he's looking for Liza.

378
00:19:21,567 --> 00:19:23,100
Come on, get in.

379
00:19:23,233 --> 00:19:25,267
We might catch Jin Ho
on the way.

380
00:19:25,867 --> 00:19:27,433
Let's go, let's go.

381
00:19:32,533 --> 00:19:34,433
[ENGINE STARTS]

382
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:40,033
[REVVING]

383
00:19:40,167 --> 00:19:44,500
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

384
00:19:57,900 --> 00:19:58,967
Follow that car.

385
00:19:59,100 --> 00:20:00,633
Yes, Sir!

386
00:20:00,767 --> 00:20:04,567
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

387
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:09,567
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

388
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:15,433
Where are we taking Liza,
Berdugo?

389
00:20:15,567 --> 00:20:18,100
Anywhere deserted we pass by.

390
00:20:18,233 --> 00:20:19,800
Hurry...

391
00:20:19,933 --> 00:20:21,900
I still have an event to attend.

392
00:20:22,033 --> 00:20:25,933
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

393
00:20:35,700 --> 00:20:39,767
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

394
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:42,333
What's the place
Jin Ho mentioned?

395
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:44,133
It could be anywhere.

396
00:20:44,267 --> 00:20:46,067
This area is huge.

397
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:49,367
Maybe we'll see him here.

398
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:52,567
We might even run into him.

399
00:20:53,567 --> 00:20:55,833
<i> We're following a subject now.</i>

400
00:20:55,967 --> 00:20:57,533
<i> Possible target.</i>

401
00:20:57,967 --> 00:20:59,633
That's Dad.

402
00:20:59,767 --> 00:21:02,867
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

403
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,733
Get ready.

404
00:21:04,867 --> 00:21:05,733
We'll block them.

405
00:21:05,867 --> 00:21:06,967
Yes, Sir!

406
00:21:07,100 --> 00:21:08,867
Who are they following?

407
00:21:09,267 --> 00:21:11,033
Could it be Jin Ho?

408
00:21:11,167 --> 00:21:15,267
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

409
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:21,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

410
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:22,300
Move!

411
00:21:22,433 --> 00:21:23,700
Hurry!

412
00:21:23,833 --> 00:21:25,933
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

413
00:21:26,067 --> 00:21:29,467
[GUN COCKING]

414
00:21:32,433 --> 00:21:36,400
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

415
00:21:39,367 --> 00:21:41,033
The Hope Circle Foundation

416
00:21:41,167 --> 00:21:44,600
will be able to build
the Angel Sanctuary.

417
00:21:44,767 --> 00:21:47,533
We would like to thank
all of you so much.

418
00:21:47,667 --> 00:21:48,933
Jin Ho, we're worried about you.

419
00:21:49,067 --> 00:21:50,600
<i> I can't go there right now.</i>

420
00:21:50,733 --> 00:21:52,467
What matters is
I get to the quarry.

421
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:53,833
Berdugo might be there.

422
00:21:53,967 --> 00:21:56,700
Someone told us the group
we're looking for is here.

423
00:21:56,833 --> 00:21:58,300
- Jin Ho!
- Berdugo!

424
00:21:58,433 --> 00:22:01,500
This day won't end
without us catching Berdugo.

425
00:22:01,633 --> 00:22:02,300
Surrender now!

426
00:22:02,433 --> 00:22:03,900
I'll give you ten seconds!

427
00:22:04,033 --> 00:22:05,267
I'm out of bullets, Berdugo.

428
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:06,900
We have no choice.
